  $$z = -\frac{27}{8} = \frac{27}{8}(\cos 180^\circ + i\sin 180^\circ), \quad n = 3$$
  $$\sqrt[3]{r} = \sqrt[3]{\frac{27}{8}} = \frac{3}{2}$$
  $$\theta_k = \frac{180^\circ + 360^\circ k}{3} = 60^\circ + 120^\circ k$$
  $$\text{Para } k = 0:$$
  $$\theta_0 = 60^\circ + 120^\circ(0) = 60^\circ$$
  $$w_0 = \frac{3}{2}(\cos 60^\circ + i\sin 60^\circ)$$
  $$w_0 = \frac{3}{2}\left(\frac{1}{2} + \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}i\right)$$
  $$w_0 = \frac{3}{4} + \frac{3\sqrt{3}}{4}i$$
  $$\text{Para } k = 1:$$
  $$\theta_1 = 60^\circ + 120^\circ(1) = 180^\circ$$
  $$w_1 = \frac{3}{2}(\cos 180^\circ + i\sin 180^\circ)$$
  $$w_1 = \frac{3}{2}(-1 + 0i)$$
  $$w_1 = -\frac{3}{2}$$
  $$\text{Para } k = 2:$$
  $$\theta_2 = 60^\circ + 120^\circ(2) = 300^\circ$$
  $$w_2 = \frac{3}{2}(\cos 300^\circ + i\sin 300^\circ)$$
  $$w_2 = \frac{3}{2}\left(\frac{1}{2} - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}i\right)$$
  $$w_2 = \frac{3}{4} - \frac{3\sqrt{3}}{4}i$$
- **Resultado:**
  $$w_0 = \frac{3}{4} + \frac{3\sqrt{3}}{4}i$$
  $$w_1 = -\frac{3}{2}$$
  $$w_2 = \frac{3}{4} - \frac{3\sqrt{3}}{4}i$$

